                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "TD;DR Small simple mobile game that fails to be worth your time on PC.\n\nWhile the game has a Castle Crashers look to it; it is far from that level of quality. Units ONLY really look good when they're very tiny on screen. Once blown up, they look like a bad flash game.\n\nLet me break it down for you...\n\n1. Still has TABLE/MOBILE resolutions that cannot be changed.\n2. Still has mention of SWIPING/TAPPING.\n3. Has no actual volume control within the game. Only Mute toggle.\n4. The \"5 special items\" should actually just be Spells but are called items so you have to buy them instead of waiting for mana. (can be purchased with in-game money but it's a hidden means to force you to buy more currency)\n5. Gameplay often results in you sitting there waiting or watching the repeatative combat until you either win or lose horribly.\n6. Even though there is a PAUSE button, the game will automatically pause if you leave the window or Alt+Tab away. This means if you're stuck waiting for a battle to complete, it will not complete without you watching.\n7. Move limit means if you're not preping for chains or doing chains you will not advance without grinding lower levels to have stronger units. Since the game cannot be sped up, auto completed or have anything to deal with grinding, it makes playing even less entertaining.\n8. Weird loading issues and fading hangs. My computer can run this game easily like it's Notepad. I cannot, for the life of me understand why the game fades to a semi-transparent black and often hangs there. Objects are still clickable and if selected will still do as they're intended.\n\nI'm sure I could go on and on about issues with the game but it's just a brainless PC port hoping to cash in on that PC dollar, dollar, with Microtransactions.\n",
